<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Honaine</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Honaine is a small port on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> coast of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a>, north-west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tlemcen">Tlemcen</a>. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> it was one of the main harbours of the Zayyanid kingdom of Tlemcen, through which goods from the Saharan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caravan-trade">caravan routes</a> were traded with European merchants. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> occupied and then destroyed it in the 1530s, and remains of its walls survive.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/honaine.jpg" alt="Honaine" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Riad Salih · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Port_de_Hona%C3%AFne.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
